 "slug": "ai-discernment",
 "title": "Improving AI Discernment: do misinformation interventions help people spot AI-generated media?",
 "authors": [
  "Yamil Velez"
 ],
 "summary": "We tested eleven interventions aimed at improving people's ability to distinguish AI-generated media from authentic content in a US survey experiment. No intervention was pre-registered; all tests are post hoc. On total discernment accuracy, Automated Flagging and AI Literacy Guide each raised accuracy by roughly 4–5 percentage points, while Mindfulness lowered it by about 4 points; the pooled effect across all arms was not distinguishable from zero. On detection of AI-generated content specifically, Breathing Exercise, AI Accuracy Nudge, and AI Literacy Guide each improved detection by 7–9 points, and the pooled effect was significant. On recognition of authentic content, only AI Literacy Infographic 2 showed a significant effect, reducing recognition by 6 points—a false-alarm cost. No pr",
